Text:
fearlessMessage is a program that sends one Message to the 'single' manager, and prints the Answer on its standard output.

Grammar:
Message ::= "Show"                                                         \
          | "Show ", ProjectName                                           \
          | "Register ", Base16                                            \
          | "Quit"                                                         \
          | "Reset"                                                        \
          | "ConnectEclipse ", Base16                                      \
          | "EditMetadata ", Base16                                        \
          | "OpenWithOrShortcut ", Base16                                  \
          | "OpenWithOrShortcut ", Base16, " ", ProjectName, " ", TypeName \
          | "Run ", ProjectName                                            \
          | "Compile ", ProjectName                                        \
          | "Check ", ProjectName                                          \
          | "Terminate ", ProjectName                                      \
          | "DeleteCache ", ProjectName                                    \
          | "Forget ", ProjectName                                         \
          | "Fix ", ProjectName                                            \
          | "Kind ", ProjectName, " ", Kind                                \
          | "Mount ", ProjectName, " ", TypeName, " ", ProjectName         \
          | "Unmount ", ProjectName, " ", TypeName                         \
          | "Attenuate ", ProjectName, " ", TypeName, SpacedTypeName1 .. SpacedTypeNamen \
          | "SelectMains ", ProjectName, SpacedTypeName1 .. SpacedTypeNamen
SpacedTypeName ::= " ", TypeName
Base16 ::= "Base16:", ([0-9A-F][0-9A-F])+
Answer ::= "Applied\n", Output | "Refused\n", Error
Output ::= the text that the message writes in the Output of its project
Error ::= the text of an error

Well formedness:
in Message: all TypeName of a SelectMains are disjoint.

Define fearlessMessage:
A The arguments of fearlessMessage, joined by one space, are the Message m.
B fearlessMessage.send(m)

Define fearlessMessage:
A The arguments of fearlessMessage, joined by one space, are not a Message.
B fearlessMessage prints on its standard error an error quoting the arguments, and listing the forms of a Message.
C fearlessMessage ends with an error.

Define fearlessMessage.send(m):
A The folder at the 'manager path' holds one LockFile, single_manager_at_X.lock, and a process holds the lock of single_manager_at_X.lock.
B fearlessMessage connects to the port X of the loopback address, and sends m.
C fearlessMessage prints on its standard output the Answer it receives, until the connection ends.
D fearlessMessage ends.

Define fearlessMessage.send(m):
A The folder at the 'manager path' holds one LockFile, no_manager.lock or candidate_manager.lock, and a process holds the lock of that LockFile.
B fearlessMessage waits until A does not hold.
C fearlessMessage.send(m)

Define fearlessMessage.send(m):
A No folder is at the 'manager path', or the folder at the 'manager path' holds no LockFile or more than one LockFile, or no process holds the lock of the LockFile of that folder.
B fearlessMessage runs fearlessManager.
C fearlessMessage waits until A does not hold, or until fearlessManager ends with no error.
D fearlessMessage.send(m)

Define fearlessMessage.send(m):
A No folder is at the 'manager path', or the folder at the 'manager path' holds no LockFile or more than one LockFile, or no process holds the lock of the LockFile of that folder.
B fearlessMessage runs fearlessManager.
C fearlessManager prints e on its standard error, and ends with an error.
D fearlessMessage prints e on its standard error, and ends with an error.

Implementation notes:
A connection is TCP on the loopback address; a Message and its Answer are UTF-8 text.
The first line fearlessMessage sends on a connection is the base16 of the 'manager path', and fearlessManager answers that line only when that line is the base16 of its own 'manager path'.
When no answer to that first line arrives within a timeout, the process on the port X is not the 'single' manager: fearlessMessage ends the connection and calls fearlessMessage.send(m) again.
fearlessManager runs in a process of its own, independent of fearlessMessage: fearlessManager does not keep the standard output and the standard error of fearlessMessage, and fearlessMessage reads e from the standard error of fearlessManager.
The bytes of a Base16 path: on Windows the UTF-16 code units of the name, little endian (a name may contain an unpaired surrogate); elsewhere the bytes of the name as the file system stores them.
